This repository contains the X2Streaming-TTS method implementation and is
released under the MIT License. It uses Qwen3TTS-Streaming as an external git
submodule; no upstream engine source is vendored into the X2Streaming-TTS
Python package.

The separate web/ demo includes MIT-licensed browser SDK and playback
components from Qwen3TTS-Streaming. See web/NOTICE and web/upstream-source.json.

Third-party source and runtime components retain their own licenses. See
THIRD_PARTY.md and the NOTICE files inside each submodule.

The optional Chinese text-normalization adapter uses WeTextProcessing
(Apache-2.0): https://github.com/wenet-e2e/WeTextProcessing

The separately distributed X2Streaming-TTS-1.7B and
X2-NativeCursor-Qwen3TTS-12Hz weights are released under Apache-2.0.
Each model repository carries its own LICENSE and NOTICE. The TTS model
derives from Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base and includes the unchanged
Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz, both released by the Qwen team under Apache-2.0.
Those weights are not distributed by this method-code repository.
